course: dictionary
lesson: 5780
title: Luxury and needs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Luxury means great comfort and expensive, beautiful things. A luxury is something nice that you do not really need, like expensive chocolate or a holiday. Think of a luxury as a treat, not a must-have.
explain: «The Rat jokes about the missing luxuries and comes back from the cellar with bottles of beer.» Luxuries is the plural of luxury, so it means more than one nice extra. The sentence does not list them, but the word jokes tells you the Rat is making light of things that are gone, and the bottles of beer show the sort of treat people enjoy.
explain: To tell a need from a luxury, ask: could I live without it? Food, water and a warm home are needs. A luxury is a want. As an adjective, luxury is used before a noun, as in «a luxury car», which means an expensive, comfortable car.
fact: Luxury means great comfort and expensive, beautiful things.
fact: A luxury is something nice that you do not really need.
fact: The plural of a luxury is luxuries.
fact: As an adjective, luxury comes before a noun, as in «a luxury hotel».
fact: In money lessons, luxuries are called wants, not needs.
exercise: What is the plural of a luxury? | luxurees | luxuri | *luxuries | luxurys
exercise: Which of these is a luxury rather than a need? | A warm coat in winter | Food for your dinner | Water to drink | *An expensive box of chocolates
exercise: In «a luxury car», what kind of word is luxury? | *An adjective, describing the car | A verb, an action word | A noun, the name of a thing | An adverb, telling how
test: A luxury is what kind of thing? | Something you must have to stay alive | Something very old | A warm, wet day | *Something nice that you do not really need
test: Which phrase uses luxury as an adjective? | luxuries are wants | *a luxury hotel | a luxury is nice | live in luxury
exam: Which of these is a need, not a luxury? | Gold-plated taps | *Clean water to drink | A holiday in the sun | A diamond ring
